  "summary": "Pachacamac is a large pre-Columbian ruin in the Lurin Valley on Peru's central coast, with major building from c. 200 BCE and a long reputation as an oracle seat and pilgrimage centre. The Incas added a Temple of the Sun, and Pizarro's soldiers sacked the shrine around 1532.",
